{#
  The requests the page makes after it has loaded.

  Nothing is stored for this: the page itself records each request it sends
  and fills the table below in the browser, linking every response to the
  profile it names. Only the page that made them can list them.
#}
{% block toolbar %}
{% from "@xtr_web_profiler/profiler/toolbar_item.html.j2" import toolbar_item %}
{% set icon %}
<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
  <path d="M8 1.6a6.4 6.4 0 1 0 6.4 6.4"></path>
  <path d="M11.4 1.8l3 1.2-1.2 3"></path>
</svg>
<span class="xtr-toolbar-value" data-xtr-ajax-count>0</span>
{% endset %}
{% set text %}
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Method</th>
      <th scope="col">Status</th>
      <th scope="col">URL</th>
      <th scope="col">Took</th>
      <th scope="col">Profile</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody data-xtr-ajax-list>
    <tr class="xtr-toolbar-empty">
      <td colspan="5">No request was sent after the page loaded.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endset %}
{{ toolbar_item(collector.name, icon, text, link=panel_url(collector.name)) }}
{% endblock %}

{% block menu %}
<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
  <path d="M8 1.6a6.4 6.4 0 1 0 6.4 6.4"></path>
  <path d="M11.4 1.8l3 1.2-1.2 3"></path>
</svg>
<span class="xtr-menu-label">Background requests</span>
{% endblock %}

{% block panel %}
<h1 class="xtr-panel-title">Background requests</h1>
<section class="xtr-card">
  <div class="xtr-card-body">
    <p>
      The requests a page sends after it has loaded are listed in the toolbar
      of that page, under this panel's icon — not here. The browser is the
      only place that sees them: it records the method, the address, how long
      each took, the status it came back with, and the profile its response
      named, so each one opens its own profile from there.
    </p>
    <p class="xtr-card-note">
      A background request gets no toolbar of its own, which is why the page
      that made it keeps the list. Paths matching the profiler's
      <code class="xtr-mono">excluded_ajax_paths</code> setting are left out,
      so the toolbar loading itself never shows up. With
      <code class="xtr-mono">ajax_replace</code> on, a background request's
      response can swap the whole toolbar for its own profile.
    </p>
    <p class="xtr-card-note">
      A failed request — a status of 400 or more, or no response at all —
      turns the toolbar's icon red until the page is loaded again.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
